// RE-BODY strikers (concept 20 section 14, review E13): one shared module used by all three lines. Hammer, Pluck
// and Breath are onset-triggered excitations that replace (or, with Blend, join) the audio-through contact.
// Detection (novelty hysteresis 0.15, refractory 30 ms, velocity from the onset peak, Touch curve) is the line's;
// this module turns one trigger into one burst.
//
// ---- Final API (namespace rebody::strikers) -------------------------------------------------------------------
//   struct StrikerState                         one per line; reset() clears it except noiseState (the line
//                                               seeds noiseState after reset, as initLine does)
//   void reset (StrikerState& s)
//   void trigger (StrikerState& s, int kind, float velocity01, float position01, float sr)
//       kind 1 Hammer, 2 Pluck (string targets), 3 Breath, 4 Pluck for non-string targets (kindPluckBody);
//       other kinds are ignored. Starts a new burst at once. A running Breath re-attacks from its current
//       envelope (no click); a running Hammer/Pluck restarts hard (with the line's 30 ms refractory only Plucks
//       below about 65 Hz can still be running). velocity01 and position01 are clamped to 0..1.
//   float step (StrikerState& s, int kind, float hz, float hold01, float sr)
//       One mono sample, DC-blocked (20 Hz) and energy-normalised. Call it every sample while active(s) (it
//       returns 0 at no cost when idle). The running burst keeps the kind it was triggered with; `kind` (the
//       line's current Excite) only matters for Breath: anything but 3 releases it. `hz` is read on the first
//       step after the trigger (Pluck period; hz <= 0 turns a Pluck into the body impulse). `hold01` is the
//       Breath sustain level 0..1 (listened component above threshold); `sr` is ignored after the trigger.
//   bool active (StrikerState& s)               burst running or its DC-blocker tail above 1e-6
//   float velocityLevel (float velocity01)      the level law below; strikeGain / throughGain: equal-power Blend
//   Wiring sketch (per sample, the line's): kind = excite == modePluck && the target is not a string ?
//   kindPluckBody : excite; on an accepted onset trigger (l.striker, kind, velocity01, position01, sr); then
//   strike = step (l.striker, excite, pitchHz, hold01, sr) and contact = strikeGain (blend) * strike (both
//   channels) + throughGain (blend) * through. Velocity carries the onset energy, so the striker needs no other
//   envelope; a caller that wants concept 14's "normalised to the listened envelope" multiplies strike by it.
//
// ---- Level law and energy normalisation --------------------------------------------------------------------
//   level = 10^(-22.22 (1 - velocity01) / 20): 0 dB at 1, -20 dB at 0.1, -22.2 dB at 0 (dB linear in velocity,
//   i.e. the force is log-mapped). A burst with velocity01 = 1 has unit RMS over its own duration:
//     Hammer, Pluck, body impulse: deterministic bursts. On the first step the burst is rendered once ahead
//       (same generator, DC blocker from zero) and the gain is level / RMS of that rendering over the burst
//       length, so the normalisation is exact and includes the DC blocker (which takes 0.4-0.8 dB off a
//       unipolar 1-3 ms pulse and much more off a 40 Hz pluck).
//     Breath: stochastic, normalised analytically: band-passed noise / its exact RMS (closed-form sum of the
//       squared impulse response of the two one-poles, uniform variance 1/3), then the reed shaping divided by
//       its measured RMS (0.6575, +-0.1 dB 44.1-192 kHz), so the sustained level at hold01 = 1 is unit RMS
//       (that is the Breath's own duration while it sustains). A Breath without hold (attack + release only,
//       linear ramps) has the same peak and an RMS of 1/sqrt(3) (-4.8 dB) over its 40-160 ms.
//   So Blend 50 (equal power, strikeGain/throughGain) is half/half against a unit-RMS Through signal.
//
// ---- Kinds ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   Hammer (PHYSIFY DSP:913-1004, :2060-2131): Hertz contact F = x^p + a d(x^p)/dt (Stulov hysteresis), p 2.5
//     (felt), a 0.25, F >= 0, integrated by symplectic Euler with 4 substeps per sample in units where mass,
//     stiffness and impact speed are 1 (x unit = (m v0^2 / K)^(1/(p+1)), time unit T = x unit / v0). The pulse
//     shape is then universal (normalised contact time 2.953); mass/stiffness only set T. Impact speed is
//     log-mapped from velocity01 over 6:1 (= the 22.2 dB level range at F ~ v0^(2p/(p+1))), so the contact
//     time is 1.2 ms x 2.155^(1 - velocity01): 1.2 ms at 1, 2.4 ms at 0.1, 2.6 ms at 0 (Hertz: tau ~ v0^-3/7).
//     Output = mean force of the 4 substeps. The burst ends when the force returns to 0 on the rebound.
//   Pluck (BODY's uke pick comb, BODY:376, :689-690): one period P = sr / hz (2..4096 samples, latched on the
//     first step) of a raised-cosine displacement hump 0.5 (1 - cos(2 pi n / P)) through the position comb
//     y = h(n) - 0.92 h(n - D), D = position01 x P (1..2048 samples, fractional). Burst length ceil(P + D).
//   Pluck body impulse (kind 4, or kind 2 with hz <= 0): one raised-cosine hump of 0.5 + 1.5 position01 ms
//     (position 0 = edge, short and bright; 1 = centre, soft); its width is the position low-pass (first
//     spectral null at 2 / width: 4 kHz .. 1 kHz).
//   Breath (BODY:615-634 gated noise, :768-803 sax reed law): xorshift noise (per-line seed noiseState)
//     band-passed as BODY's sax breath (one-pole 4.2 kHz minus one-pole 450 Hz), normalised to unit RMS, then
//     BODY's asymmetric reed shaping q = 0.65 clamp(u, -4, 4), 1.55 (q / (1 + 0.6 |q|) + 0.12 q^2 / (1 + q^2)),
//     times a linear envelope: attack to the level in A, then the envelope follows level x hold01 (rise over A,
//     fall over R per full level), A = R = 80 - 60 velocity01 ms (20 ms at 1, 74 ms at 0.1). The burst ends
//     when the envelope is 0 and hold01 is 0. The even term adds DC in proportion to the envelope; the DC
//     blocker removes it.
//   Every kind: DC blocker y = x - x[-1] + r y[-1], r = exp(-2 pi 20 / sr) (E13: unipolar pulses carry DC); the
//   sum of a whole burst including its tail is 0 by construction. After the burst the tail rings down
//   (about 100 ms to 1e-6 after a hammer); active() stays true until then.
//
// ---- State size and cost -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   StrikerState: 4 int + 1 bool + 22 float + 6 float64 = 39 words (156 bytes) per line, no buffers (the comb
//   reads the analytic hump at n - D instead of a delay line).
//   Per sample while a burst runs (flops): Hammer 4 x (sqrt + 14) about 60 + 4 sqrt; Pluck 18 (float64 phasor);
//   body impulse 10; Breath about 30 + 2 divisions (xorshift, two one-poles, shaping, envelope); DC blocker 3.
//   Idle: three compares. Tail only: 4 + compares.
//   Per trigger (the look-ahead runs inside the first step(), one spike per strike): velocityLevel (one pow), DC
//   radius (one exp); Hammer one pow + the look-ahead of its 58-125 samples at 48 kHz (about 7 k flops and 500
//   sqrt); Pluck float64 cos/sin twice + the look-ahead of P + D samples (about 18 flops each: 15 k at 110 Hz,
//   worst case 110 k at P = 4096, D = 2048); Breath two exp and one sqrt.

namespace rebody::strikers
{
    // Values of the Excite parameter (spec.json param12/35/58: Through|Hammer|Pluck|Breath).
    const int modeThrough = 0;
    const int modeHammer = 1;
    const int modePluck = 2;
    const int modeBreath = 3;

    // trigger() kinds: the Excite values plus the Pluck variant for non-string targets.
    const int kindHammer = 1;
    const int kindPluck = 2;
    const int kindBreath = 3;
    const int kindPluckBody = 4;

    const float velocityRangeDb = 22.222222f;  // level at velocity 0 (dB below velocity 1); 0.1 -> -20 dB
    const float dcHz = 20.0f;
    const float tailFloor = 0.000001f;         // DC-blocker tail below this ends active()

    const float hammerHysteresis = 0.25f;      // Stulov alpha in units of T
    const float hammerSpan = 2.95315f;         // contact duration of the normalised pulse (p 2.5, a 0.25)
    const float hammerFastest = 0.0012f;       // contact time at velocity 1, seconds
    const float hammerRatio = 2.1553f;         // contact time ratio velocity 0 / velocity 1 = 6^(3/7)
    const int lookAheadLimit = 8192;           // safety cap of the look-ahead rendering

    const float pluckCombGain = 0.92f;         // BODY:690
    const float pluckMaxPeriod = 4096.0f;
    const float pluckMaxDelay = 2048.0f;
    const float bodyImpulseShortest = 0.0005f;
    const float bodyImpulseLongest = 0.002f;

    const float breathFastest = 0.020f;        // attack/release at velocity 1, seconds
    const float breathSlowest = 0.080f;        // ... at velocity 0
    const float breathLowHz = 4200.0f;         // BODY:536-538 sax breath band
    const float breathHighHz = 450.0f;
    const float reedDrive = 0.65f;             // BODY sax reed law (:787-788)
    const float reedSoft = 0.60f;
    const float reedEven = 0.12f;
    const float reedGain = 1.55f;
    const float reedClamp = 4.0f;
    const float reedRms = 0.6575f;             // RMS of the shaped unit noise after DC removal (measured)

    struct StrikerState
    {
        int kind;                  // kind of the running burst, 0 = none (the DC tail may still ring)
        int age;                   // samples since the trigger (0 = set-up pending on the next step)
        int length;                // burst length in samples; 0 = not known yet (Hammer in contact, Breath)
        bool sustaining;           // Breath: attack finished, the envelope follows hold01
        float velocity, position, level, gain, sr;
        float xi, eta, xpPrev, substep;                    // Hammer: normalised Hertz contact
        float period, delay;                               // Pluck: hump length and comb delay (samples)
        float64 pc, ps, rotC, rotS, delayCos, delaySin;    // Pluck: raised-cosine phasor
        float envelope, attackStep, releaseStep;           // Breath envelope (per-sample steps)
        float noiseLow, noiseHigh, lowCoef, highCoef, noiseNorm;
        float dcRadius, dcPrevious, dcState;               // DC blocker
        int noiseState;                                    // xorshift state for Breath (seeded per line)
    }

    void reset (StrikerState& s)
    {
        s.kind = 0;
        s.age = 0;
        s.length = 0;
        s.sustaining = false;
        s.velocity = 0.0f;
        s.position = 0.0f;
        s.level = 0.0f;
        s.gain = 0.0f;
        s.sr = 0.0f;                           // set by trigger()
        s.xi = 0.0f;
        s.eta = 0.0f;
        s.xpPrev = 0.0f;
        s.substep = 0.0f;
        s.period = 0.0f;
        s.delay = 0.0f;
        s.pc = 1.0;
        s.ps = 0.0;
        s.rotC = 1.0;
        s.rotS = 0.0;
        s.delayCos = 1.0;
        s.delaySin = 0.0;
        s.envelope = 0.0f;
        s.attackStep = 0.0f;
        s.releaseStep = 0.0f;
        s.noiseLow = 0.0f;
        s.noiseHigh = 0.0f;
        s.lowCoef = 0.0f;
        s.highCoef = 0.0f;
        s.noiseNorm = 0.0f;
        s.dcRadius = 0.0f;
        s.dcPrevious = 0.0f;
        s.dcState = 0.0f;
    }

    // Level law: dB linear in velocity, 0 dB at 1, -20 dB at 0.1.
    float velocityLevel (float velocity01)
    {
        return rebody::analysis::dbToGain (-velocityRangeDb * (1.0f - clamp (velocity01, 0.0f, 1.0f)));
    }

    // BODY's asymmetric reed shaping on a unit-RMS signal (BODY:787-788).
    float reedShape (float u)
    {
        float q = reedDrive * clamp (u, -reedClamp, reedClamp);
        return reedGain * (q / (1.0f + reedSoft * abs (q)) + reedEven * q * q / (1.0f + q * q));
    }

    void trigger (StrikerState& s, int kind, float velocity01, float position01, float sr)
    {
        if (kind < kindHammer || kind > kindPluckBody)
            return;

        float rate = max (sr, 1000.0f);
        float v = clamp (rebody::analysis::finiteOrZero (velocity01), 0.0f, 1.0f);
        bool breathRunning = s.kind == kindBreath;

        s.kind = kind;
        s.age = 0;
        s.length = 0;
        s.velocity = v;
        s.position = clamp (rebody::analysis::finiteOrZero (position01), 0.0f, 1.0f);
        s.sr = rate;
        s.level = velocityLevel (v);
        s.gain = 0.0f;
        s.dcRadius = rebody::analysis::dcBlockRadius (dcHz, rate);

        if (kind == kindBreath)
        {
            if (! breathRunning)
            {
                s.envelope = 0.0f;
                s.noiseLow = 0.0f;
                s.noiseHigh = 0.0f;
            }

            float seconds = breathSlowest + (breathFastest - breathSlowest) * v;
            s.attackStep = s.level / (seconds * rate);
            s.releaseStep = s.attackStep;
            s.sustaining = false;
            s.lowCoef = rebody::analysis::onePoleCoefficient (breathLowHz, rate);
            s.highCoef = rebody::analysis::onePoleCoefficient (breathHighHz, rate);

            // Sum of h^2 of h = a1 b1^n - a2 b2^n (b = 1 - a): the band-pass gain on white noise.
            float a1 = s.lowCoef;
            float a2 = s.highCoef;
            float b1 = 1.0f - a1;
            float b2 = 1.0f - a2;
            float sumSquares = a1 * a1 / (1.0f - b1 * b1) + a2 * a2 / (1.0f - b2 * b2) - 2.0f * a1 * a2 / (1.0f - b1 * b2);
            s.noiseNorm = 1.0f / float (sqrt (max (sumSquares / 3.0f, 1.0e-12f)));
            s.gain = 1.0f / reedRms;
        }
    }

    // ---- generators: raw (pre-DC, unit-scale) sample at s.age; they advance their own state ----------------

    float hammerRaw (StrikerState& s)
    {
        if (s.length > 0)
            return 0.0f;

        float h = s.substep;
        float force = 0.0f;

        for (int k = 0; k < 4; k += 1)
        {
            float x = max (s.xi, 0.0f);
            float xp = x * x * float (sqrt (x));
            float f = max (0.0f, xp + hammerHysteresis * (xp - s.xpPrev) / h);
            s.xpPrev = xp;
            s.eta -= f * h;
            s.xi += s.eta * h;
            force += 0.25f * f;

            if (f == 0.0f && s.eta < 0.0f)
            {
                s.length = s.age + 1;
                break;
            }
        }

        return force;
    }

    float pluckRaw (StrikerState& s)
    {
        float n = float (s.age);
        float hump = n < s.period ? 0.5f - 0.5f * float (s.pc) : 0.0f;
        float shifted = 0.0f;

        if (n >= s.delay && n < s.delay + s.period)
            shifted = 0.5f - 0.5f * float (s.pc * s.delayCos + s.ps * s.delaySin);

        float64 c = s.pc * s.rotC - s.ps * s.rotS;
        s.ps = s.pc * s.rotS + s.ps * s.rotC;
        s.pc = c;
        return hump - pluckCombGain * shifted;
    }

    float breathRaw (StrikerState& s, float hold)
    {
        if (! s.sustaining)
        {
            s.envelope = min (s.envelope + s.attackStep, max (s.level, s.envelope));

            if (s.envelope >= s.level)
                s.sustaining = true;
        }
        else
        {
            float target = s.level * clamp (hold, 0.0f, 1.0f);

            if (s.envelope < target)
                s.envelope = min (target, s.envelope + s.attackStep);
            else
                s.envelope = max (target, s.envelope - s.releaseStep);

            if (s.envelope <= 0.0f && target <= 0.0f)
            {
                s.envelope = 0.0f;
                s.length = s.age + 1;
            }
        }

        s.noiseState = rebody::analysis::xorshift (s.noiseState);
        float noise = rebody::analysis::noiseOf (s.noiseState);
        s.noiseLow += s.lowCoef * (noise - s.noiseLow);
        s.noiseHigh += s.highCoef * (noise - s.noiseHigh);
        return s.envelope * reedShape ((s.noiseLow - s.noiseHigh) * s.noiseNorm);
    }

    float deterministicRaw (StrikerState& s)
    {
        if (s.kind == kindHammer)
            return hammerRaw (s);

        return pluckRaw (s);
    }

    float dcBlock (StrikerState& s, float x)
    {
        float y = x - s.dcPrevious + s.dcRadius * s.dcState;
        s.dcPrevious = x;
        s.dcState = y;
        return y;
    }

    // Look-ahead: render the deterministic burst once (unit gain, DC blocker from zero) and return the gain that
    // gives the burst RMS = level over its own length.
    float normaliserFor (StrikerState& s)
    {
        StrikerState c = s;
        c.dcPrevious = 0.0f;
        c.dcState = 0.0f;
        float64 energy = 0.0;

        for (int n = 0; n < lookAheadLimit; n += 1)
        {
            float y = dcBlock (c, deterministicRaw (c));
            energy += float64 (y) * float64 (y);
            c.age += 1;

            if (c.length > 0 && c.age >= c.length)
                break;
        }

        float meanSquare = float (energy / float64 (max (c.age, 1)));
        return meanSquare > 1.0e-20f ? s.level / float (sqrt (meanSquare)) : 0.0f;
    }

    // First step after a trigger: everything that needs hz, then the normaliser.
    void setUp (StrikerState& s, float hz)
    {
        if (s.kind == kindBreath)
            return;

        if (s.kind == kindHammer)
        {
            float contact = hammerFastest * float (pow (hammerRatio, 1.0f - s.velocity));
            s.xi = 0.0f;
            s.eta = 1.0f;
            s.xpPrev = 0.0f;
            s.substep = 0.25f * hammerSpan / (contact * max (s.sr, 1000.0f));
            s.length = 0;
        }
        else
        {
            bool onString = s.kind == kindPluck && hz > 0.0f;

            if (onString)
            {
                s.period = clamp (s.sr / max (hz, 0.001f), 2.0f, pluckMaxPeriod);
                s.delay = clamp (s.position * s.period, 1.0f, pluckMaxDelay);
                s.length = int (float (ceil (s.period + s.delay)));
            }
            else
            {
                s.kind = kindPluckBody;
                s.period = max (2.0f, (bodyImpulseShortest + (bodyImpulseLongest - bodyImpulseShortest) * s.position) * s.sr);
                s.delay = 1.0e9f;
                s.length = int (float (ceil (s.period)));
            }

            float64 w = twoPi / float64 (s.period);
            s.pc = 1.0;
            s.ps = 0.0;
            s.rotC = cos (w);
            s.rotS = sin (w);
            s.delayCos = onString ? cos (w * float64 (s.delay)) : 1.0;
            s.delaySin = onString ? sin (w * float64 (s.delay)) : 0.0;
        }

        s.gain = normaliserFor (s);
    }

    float step (StrikerState& s, int kind, float hz, float hold01, float sr)
    {
        if (s.kind == 0)
        {
            if (s.dcState == 0.0f && s.dcPrevious == 0.0f)
                return 0.0f;

            float tail = dcBlock (s, 0.0f);

            if (abs (tail) < tailFloor)
            {
                s.dcState = 0.0f;
                s.dcPrevious = 0.0f;
            }

            return tail;
        }

        if (s.age == 0)
            setUp (s, rebody::analysis::finiteOrZero (hz));

        float raw = 0.0f;

        if (s.kind == kindBreath)
            raw = breathRaw (s, kind == modeBreath ? rebody::analysis::finiteOrZero (hold01) : 0.0f);
        else
            raw = deterministicRaw (s);

        float y = dcBlock (s, s.gain * raw);
        s.age += 1;

        if (s.length > 0 && s.age >= s.length)
            s.kind = 0;

        return y;
    }

    bool active (StrikerState& s)
    {
        return s.kind != 0 || s.dcState != 0.0f || s.dcPrevious != 0.0f;
    }

    // Equal-power Blend law (Blend 0..100 %): 0 = striker alone, 100 = Through alone (concept 14).
    float strikeGain (float blendPercent)
    {
        return float (cos (0.5f * float (pi) * clamp (blendPercent, 0.0f, 100.0f) * 0.01f));
    }

    float throughGain (float blendPercent)
    {
        return float (sin (0.5f * float (pi) * clamp (blendPercent, 0.0f, 100.0f) * 0.01f));
    }
}
